<p>Cylance, now part of BlackBerry, pioneered the use of artificial intelligence in endpoint security. Its predictive AI approach prevents malware and threats before they can execute, rather than relying on signatures or behavioral analysis after the fact.</p>
<p>The platform uses mathematical models trained on billions of file characteristics to identify malicious code with high accuracy. This approach requires minimal system resources and works effectively even without internet connectivity.</p>
